commenti.body:
A flawed POV character is pretty common for Japan, most common being generally flawed but really kind, a hardworker, and/or have some special trait/ability. Tsukino Usagi (Sailor Moon), Shimura Shinpachi (Gintama), Doremi (Ojamajo Doremi), early Naruto (Naruto), etc. are some examples.

&#x200B;

More adult themes/characters in kid's media like the blue from sadness Doraemon aren't uncommon either. Gegege no Kitaro is a staple of children's anime and the sidekick character there is Medama-oyaji, an eyeball with arms and legs who was reborn from the decaying corpse of Kitaro's dead monster father. This year the Precure franchise that has 4\~9 year old girls as part of it's core demographic had a scene this season where a villain tried to kidnap a baby and ended up trembling in fear, hyperventilating, and running away at the magical girl angrily yelling and approaching him to physically beat the shit out of him.
